\chapter{Introduction}
Fatigue cracking limits the service life of welded joints. This report reviews two assessment families for bridge welds.
\begin{itemize}
\item Stress-life approaches use nominal stress ranges from design codes.
\item Fracture mechanics approaches track crack growth from an initial flaw.

\chapter{Method}
We model crack growth with the Paris law $da/dN = C\,\Delta K^m$ and integrate it numerically over the service spectrum.
The threshold $\Delta K_{th}$ marks the onset of stable growth, and the critical stress intensity $K_c = 60\,\mathrm{MPa}\sqrt{m}$ marks fast fracture.

